The applicant must be a permanent resident of the state of Tripura. The applicant must be an accredited working journalist by the state government or by the Press Information Bureau (PIB). The age of the applicant must be in between 21 years and 65 years. The applicant must not have been covered under the Ayushman Bharat Scheme or any other Health Insurance Scheme of the Central or State Government.
Exclusions / Ineligibility:
The scheme does not include any such person who--is employed mainly in a managerial or administrative capacity, orbeing employed in a supervisory capacity, performs, either by the nature of the duties attached to his office or by reason of the powers vested in him, functions mainly of a managerial nature;

